WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.007
FedRAMP High is an ongoing operational commitment, not a one-time documentation project.

00:00:05.007 --> 00:00:08.687
After authorization support work, the system continues to change.

00:00:08.687 --> 00:00:12.776
Vulnerabilities are discovered, configurations drift, staff roles change, incidents occur,

00:00:12.776 --> 00:00:16.456
dependencies evolve, and new features may alter the boundary.

00:00:16.456 --> 00:00:22.589
Continuous monitoring is the discipline that keeps security posture visible as the live system changes.

00:00:22.589 --> 00:00:25.860
Continuous monitoring includes vulnerability management, configuration drift detection,

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:30.767
change management, incident reporting expectations at a high level, periodic evidence updates,

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:34.447
risk tracking, plans of action and milestones, resilience monitoring,

00:00:34.447 --> 00:00:37.718
privileged activity review, security metrics, and operational ownership.

00:00:37.718 --> 00:00:43.442
The details may evolve, but the principle is durable: risk must be watched, reported,

00:00:43.442 --> 00:00:45.078
and managed over time.

00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:47.940
High-impact operations require stronger attention to resilience.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:52.029
Teams should understand backup and recovery expectations, dependency failure modes,

00:00:52.029 --> 00:00:53.664
monitoring coverage, escalation paths,

00:00:53.664 --> 00:00:57.344
and how critical services continue or recover during disruption.

00:00:57.344 --> 00:01:01.842
Resilience does not replace access control, incident response, or vulnerability management.

00:01:01.842 --> 00:01:07.976
It complements them by reducing the chance that a failure becomes a severe mission disruption.

00:01:07.976 --> 00:01:10.429
Continuous monitoring also supports federal trust.

00:01:10.429 --> 00:01:15.744
Authorizing officials and agency customers need confidence that the provider can identify problems,

00:01:15.744 --> 00:01:19.424
communicate risk, remediate weaknesses, and keep control evidence current.

00:01:19.424 --> 00:01:24.331
A High baseline raises the stakes for that trust because the consequences

00:01:24.331 --> 00:01:26.376
of failure are more serious.

00:01:26.376 --> 00:01:29.647
The operating model needs to show sustained discipline,

00:01:29.647 --> 00:01:32.100
not a single successful assessment moment.
